[* Q: [role dddgreen c++: What is the solution of virtual derivation grandpa constructing propagation problem?]]

[* A: [role ddred The solution is very simple: delete default constructor of the very super-base class.]]

[h1:cpp-exa-co [role cyan c++ example Code]]

[* [role ddblue // code-(1)]]

[!c++]
```
#include <iostream>

namespace manda
{
	// The very super-base class.
	class grandpa
	{
	protected:
		int x{0};
	public:
		grandpa() = delete;
		grandpa(int x): x{x} {}
	};

	class father:
		virtual public grandpa
	{
	protected:
		int y{0};
	public:
		father(int x, int y):
			grandpa{x},
			y{y}
		{}
	};

	class man:
		public father
	{
	protected:
		int z{0};
	public:
		man(int x, int y, int z):
			grandpa{x},
			father{x, y},
			z{z}
		{}
	public:
		void print() const
		{
			std::cout
				<< "(x, y, z) = "
				<< "(" <<  x << ", " << y << ", " << z << ")"
				<< std::endl
			;
		}
	};
}

int main()
{
	manda::man man{7, 4, 9};
	man.print();
}
```

[*Output:]

```
(x, y, z) = (7, 4, 9)
```

[h1:what-will-if-xxk [role cyan What will happen if man does not propagate grandpa?]]

[* [role dred What will happen if constructor of manda::man does not propagate to manda::grandpa?]]

[* [role ddblue // code-(2)]]

[!c++]
```
class man
	public father
{
private:
	int z{0};
public:
	man(int x, int y, int z):
		// grandpa{x},
		father{x, y},
		z{z}
	{}

		...
	...
};
```

[* [role ddgreen The compiling will help you to correct code by an error message:]]

[pre
error: use of deleted function ‘manda::grandpa::grandpa()
]

[h1:wha-is-dpa-prob [role cyan What is the problem?]]

[* [role dred What is the virtual derivation grandpa constructing propagation problem?]]

[* [role ddgreen
When c++ cascaded virtual derivation is enabled,[br]
manda::man constructor transfers parameters to manda::father constructor,[br]
we expect then the manda::father constructor will transfer parameters to manda::grandpa constructor,[br]
however it does not work:[br]
manda::father constructor does not transfer parameters to manda::grandpa constructor,[br]
[role ddred Because] they are virtual derivation ![br]
Instead, manda::man constructor will implicitly call a default constructor of manda::grandpa directly,[br]
which will let wrong parameters be transferred:
]]

[* [role red Like code-(2). (and if the default constructor of manda::grandpa is not deleted.)]]

[* [role dddblue
To let the correct parameters be transferred from manda::man constructor to manda::grandpa constructor,[br]
we can let the manda::man consructor propagate manda::grandpa constructor explicitly:
]]

// code-(3)
[!c++]
```
class man
	public father
{
private:
	int z{0};
public:
	man(int x, int y, int z):
		grandpa{x}, // explicit propagate
		father{x, y},
		z{z}
	{}

		...
	...
};
```

[* [role ddred However, it has an easy-to-make-mistake problem:[br]
user programming will be more easy to miss propagating to grandpa constructor,[br]
and especially, if the grandpa code is coded at a third-party library,[br]
user programming will not realize it at all.
]]

[* [role dblue The solution is delete the default constructor of grandpa like this article,[br]
then the compiling will point out the error by an error message.
]]

